    "navGroup": "Exact task-group membership follows section 1 of 03-PAGINAS-FEATURES-EN-ACTIES.md; descendants normally inherit their logical parent's task group, except settings/checklists, which remains a settings child while being a primary Quality and checklists destination.",
    "parentId": "The nearest route-level list, dossier, editor, settings index or flow owner is the parent; nested detail/editor routes form an explicit acyclic chain.",
    "navOrder": "The explicit routeIdsByGroup sequence is materialized as positive increments of 10, leaving deterministic insertion space without consumer-local sorting.",
    "navLabel": "Primary/support destinations use the approved labels in the IA table; every contextual route copies routes.json.title.",
    "icon": "A route uses its explicit task icon when declared by this contract and otherwise inherits the nearest parent icon.",
    "matchPrefixes": "Visible static destinations other than the exact root / use their literal route; settings additionally owns both /settings and /instellingen. Contextual dynamic/static descendants rely on exact route-pattern resolution and therefore use an empty prefix array.",
    "breadcrumb": "Copy routes.json.title exactly; the full trail is derived only through parentId.",
    "helpAndSearch": "Contextual descendants inherit the nearest declared logical root context. Auth routes intentionally use null because they expose neither in-product help nor command-palette search.",
    "releaseVisibility": "Destinations named in the eight-group IA table are primary, Profile/Help/Roadmap/Releases are support and every detail/editor/flow route is hidden."
  },
